    # v388 (2026-10-06) -- BESIDE: beta runs with the scale, bounded below (the stone TheCouplingRunsBoundedBelow; the operator's coinage by sha256); the erratum
    # beside «alpha is observed, not derived» (form vs number); PHASE 9 OPENED by the frozen function. The operator's quotations VERBATIM in Portuguese, translations
    # OUTSIDE the quotes; numbers READ from the core records; proved is not confirmed; not-falsified is never confirmation; the gate does not move.
    _br8 = core.get("beta_runs_bounded_below_v388") or {}
    _ho8 = core.get("hubble_ratio_opening_v388") or {}
    _nu8 = _ho8.get("numbers") or {}
    _lb8 = _nu8.get("lnB") or {}

    def _tx8(x_):
        t_ = str(x_)
        for a_, b_ in (("\\", r"\textbackslash{}"), ("_", r"\_"), ("%", r"\%"), ("&", r"\&"), ("#", r"\#"), ("$", r"\$"), ("{", r"\{"), ("}", r"\}"), ("~", r"\~{}"), ("^", r"\^{}")):
            t_ = t_.replace(a_, b_)
        return t_

    def _n8(x_, nd_=2):
        if not isinstance(x_, (int, float)) or isinstance(x_, bool) or x_ != x_:
            return r"\text{n/a}"
        return "%%.%df" % nd_ % float(x_)
    _tk8 = lambda x_: r"\texttt{" + _tx8(x_).replace(r"\_", r"\_\allowbreak{}") + "}"
    _zl8 = _nu8.get("z_por_leitor") or {}
    s.append(r"\section*{Beside (v388): $\beta$ runs with the scale, bounded below; Phase 9 opened}")
    s.append(r"\addcontentsline{toc}{section}{Beside (v388): $\beta$ runs with the scale, bounded below; Phase 9 opened}")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The coinage.} On 2026-10-06 the operator wrote that ``o alpha do betatgl é a constante da estrutura fina, mas como índice de escala da fronteira, e betatgl é a sua conjugação'' "
             r"(\emph{the alpha of beta\_TGL is the fine-structure constant, but as the scale index of the boundary, and beta\_TGL is its conjugation}) and that ``o valor de Betatgl é escalar, mas limitado inferiormente'' "
             r"(\emph{the value of beta\_TGL is scalar, but bounded below}); and, on the operation he sees in $\bTGL$ and in the Half-Nat: ``vai dividindo um número pela sua metade de modo infinito e assim, nunca chega-se ao limite'' "
             r"(\emph{dividing a number by its half infinitely, never reaching the limit}) --- ``o custo do zero absoluto é o pagamento da existência (haja luz)'' (\emph{the cost of the absolute zero is the payment of existence}). "
             r"The stone \texttt{TheCouplingRunsBoundedBelow} (" + _n8(_br8.get("kernel_flags_ok"), 0) + r" of " + _n8(_br8.get("kernel_flags_total"), 0)
             + r" declarations within the axiom trio) proves the mathematics: with $\alpha(\chi)=\mathrm{sech}(\chi/2)$ --- the closed form the program already uses --- $\alpha$ and $\beta(\chi)=\alpha(\chi)\sqrt e$ are "
             r"strictly decreasing in the depth $\chi$; the \emph{floor} sits at the supremum of $\chi$, the infrared, and is attained only there; in the domain of the sealed coupling this $\beta$ is, by definition, that of \texttt{couplingOfAlpha}; "
             r"the sum of the halves $\sum_{k<n}2^{-(k+1)}=1-2^{-n}$ is below 1 at every finite step and has limit 1; and the Half-Nat is the fixed point $x=1-x$. "
             r"In numbers: $\beta_0=\alpha_{\rm Thomson}\sqrt e=" + _n8(_br8.get("beta0"), 10) + r"$ is the \emph{boundary} constant (this paper's Scale Theorem: a type-$\mathrm{III}_1$ boundary selects Thomson); "
             r"$\beta(\mu)=\alpha(\mu)\sqrt e$ is the \emph{bulk reading} at each scale, never below the floor: at $M_Z$, $" + _n8(_br8.get("beta_MZ_on_shell"), 6) + r"$ (the Scale Theorem's one-loop $1/\alpha(M_Z)$) and $"
             + _n8(_br8.get("beta_MZ_msbar"), 6) + r"$ ($\overline{\rm MS}$, \textsf{[KNOWN]}, not checked on disk). What stays \textsf{[INPUT/ONTO]}: that the physical $\alpha$ is the $\mathrm{sech}$ of a depth growing towards the infrared; "
             r"\textsf{[KNOWN]}: that $\alpha(\mu)$ grows with $\mu$; \textsf{[OPEN]}: which $\mu$ each rite uses. The operator's sentence on the patents with a variable $\beta$ stays \textsf{[DECLARADO]}: the link was not located in the Central's files. "
             r"\textbf{Erratum beside:} where this paper says \emph{$\alpha$ is observed, not derived}, it reads: what is derived is the \emph{form} ($\alpha$ as the scale index; $\beta$ as its conjugation), not the \emph{number}, "
             r"which is still read from CODATA. Record: " + _tk8(_br8.get("verdict") or "ABSENT") + r".")
    s.append(r"\textbf{Phase 9 opened.} By the operator's order, the Hubble ratio was opened by the preregistration's \emph{frozen verdict function} (the runner hashed before opening); the program read the result by hash and "
             r"\emph{re-executed} the function on the recorded input " + (r"--- the same verdict: " if _ho8.get("same_verdict") is True else r"--- \textbf{the verdict was NOT reproduced in this run}: ")
             + _tk8(_ho8.get("verdict_of_the_frozen_function") or "n/a") + r". The local readers remain \textsf{[DECLARADO]} until the sources by sha256"
             + (r"; with them so, rule 1 of the preregistration returns what it returned, and that is the result. " if _ho8.get("same_verdict") is True else r". ")
             + r"The numbers: background $" + _n8(_nu8.get("H0_bg"), 3) + r"$, local prediction $" + _n8(_nu8.get("H0_local_previsto"), 3) + r"$, mean of the locals $" + _n8(_nu8.get("media_GLS_locais"), 3) + r"\pm" + _n8(_nu8.get("sigma_GLS_locais"), 3)
             + r"$ km/s/Mpc; $z_\delta=" + _n8(_nu8.get("z_delta")) + r"$; $z_{\rm disc}=" + _n8(_nu8.get("z_disc")) + r"$; $\ln B$(TGL/$\Lambda$CDM) $=" + _n8(_lb8.get("TGL_vs_LCDM")) + r"$, (TGL/free $\beta$) $=" + _n8(_lb8.get("TGL_vs_beta_livre"))
             + r"$ (quadrature error $" + _n8((_ho8.get("recalculo_ao_lado") or {}).get("erro_quadratura_n25_n35")) + r"$; converged $" + _n8((_ho8.get("recalculo_ao_lado") or {}).get("lnB_TGL_vs_beta_livre_convergido")) + r"$, recomputed beside"
             + r"), (TGL/Cepheid shift) $=" + _n8(_lb8.get("TGL_vs_shift_cefeidas")) + r"$, (TGL/background with free $r_d$) $=" + _n8(_lb8.get("TGL_vs_fundo_livre")) + r"$; the TRGB/CCHP at $" + _n8((_zl8.get("L2_cchp") or {}).get("z_vs_TGL"))
             + r"\sigma$ from the prediction. And the counterfactual, stated and \emph{not} a verdict: if the sources by hash confirmed the declared values, the same function would return " + _tk8(_ho8.get("counterfactual_with_sources_NOT_a_verdict") or "n/a")
             + (r" --- under this preregistration the Hubble ratio does \emph{not discriminate} at $5\sigma$ today. " if (_ho8.get("same_verdict") is True and "NOT_DISCRIMINATED_FROM_LCDM" in str(_ho8.get("counterfactual_with_sources_NOT_a_verdict"))) else r". ")
             + r"Beside: the runner marginalizes the background (the preregistration said \emph{profiled}) and reads $z_\delta$ from $-2\ln L$ with the log-det (the preregistration: $\Delta\chi^2=1$) --- a negligible measured difference ($z_{\rm disc}$ "
             + _n8((_ho8.get("recalculo_ao_lado") or {}).get("z_disc_forma_quadratica"), 4) + r" against " + _n8((_ho8.get("recalculo_ao_lado") or {}).get("z_disc_com_logdet"), 4)
             + r"); and the background with $r_d$ free only in the BAO is a weak alternative, not an early-physics analysis. Record: " + _tk8(_ho8.get("verdict") or "ABSENT") + r".")
